dd "29a84886-3c12-5e30-b049-a6317548bbd1" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $10x+2y=4$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10x+2y &= 4 \\\\\n2y &= -10x+4 \\\\\ny &= -5x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-5$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x-2y=10 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-5x-5 \\\\\n3x-3y=12 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=x-4 \\\\\n-4x-3y=9 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{4}{3}x-3 \\\\\n2x-2y=-10 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=x+5 \\\\\n5x+y=2 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-5x+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $5x+y=2$ has both the same slope $-5$ and the same $y$-intercept $2$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-10x-2y=10$ has slope $-5$ and $y$-intercept $-5$, different from $2$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-10x-2y=10\n$$"] [:db/add "29a84886-3c12-5e30-b049-a6317548bbd1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "29a84886-3c12-5e30-b049-a6317548bbd1" :question/answer-fields "7330a77d-3907-5303-8822-5cebfc03a711"] [:db/ensure "29a84886-3c12-5e30-b049-a6317548bbd1" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186087687 :knowledge-point/questions "29a84886-3c12-5e30-b049-a6317548bbd1"] [:db/add "9c459858-3eb2-5fdb-9795-f3ee4086086f" :answer/id #uuid "9c459858-3eb2-5fdb-9795-f3ee4086086f"] [:db/add "9c459858-3eb2-5fdb-9795-f3ee4086086f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9c459858-3eb2-5fdb-9795-f3ee4086086f" :answer/value "4x+6y=-30"] [:db/ensure "9c459858-3eb2-5fdb-9795-f3ee4086086f" :answer/validate] [:db/add "636f4082-c44a-549b-ba99-7415e452024f" :answer/id #uuid "636f4082-c44a-549b-ba99-7415e452024f"] [:db/add "636f4082-c44a-549b-ba99-7415e452024f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "636f4082-c44a-549b-ba99-7415e452024f" :answer/value