f8e6f505c6"] [:db/ensure "066af54e-4514-5447-9fd7-c69d34adacad" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" :question/id #uuid "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64"] [:db/add "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" :question/problem "Which of the following is a distinct line parallel to $2x+3y=-15$?"] [:db/add "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" :question/worked-solution "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $2x+3y=-15$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x+3y &= -15 \\\\\n3y &= -2x-15 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{2}{3}x-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nRewrite the choices in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x+6y=-30 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-5 \\\\\n-4x+6y=-24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x-4 \\\\\n-3x-6y=12 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{1}{2}x-2 \\\\\n-4x+6y=24 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4 \\\\\n-6x-9y=0 &\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y=-\\frac{2}{3}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe line $4x+6y=-30$ has both the same slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and the same $y$-intercept $-5$ as the given line. It is the same line, so it is not a distinct parallel line.\n\nThe line $-6x-9y=0$ has slope $-\\frac{2}{3}$ and $y$-intercept $0$, different from $-5$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\n-6x-9y=0\n$$"] [:db/add "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" :question/answer-fields "066af54e-4514-5447-9fd7-c69d34adacad"] [:db/ensure "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186087687 :knowledge-point/questions "ccc0b544-1bb9-5c7b-86fb-fc4b22388c64"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "3e16e2f7-3c42-563a-89e9-76471de5f4b5"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/script "gener